        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-1524] The firewall running on the SECC shall be configured to allow access to this (these) dedicated VAS port(s).",
            "block_bbox": [
                69,
                167,
                1052,
                221
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 1,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    69.0,
                    167.0
                ],
                [
                    1052.0,
                    167.0
                ],
                [
                    1052.0,
                    221.0
                ],
                [
                    69.0,
                    221.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-1525] Either full-handshake TLS or resumed TLS can be used to open an additional communication channel for a VAS. The resumption shall be based on the TLS context (i.e. ticket) exchanged in the V2G session. TLS session resumption shall be performed using the mechanism described in 7.7.3.7.",
            "block_bbox": [
                69,
                242,
                1053,
                348
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    69.0,
                    242.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    242.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    348.0
                ],
                [
                    69.0,
                    348.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-1527] If the SECC allows TLS resumption for VAS, the SECC shall issue the EVCC a separate TLS session ticket for each offered VAS.",
            "block_bbox": [
                69,
                370,
                1053,
                423
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    69.0,
                    370.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    370.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    423.0
                ],
                [
                    69.0,
                    423.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The SECC can provide TCP-level forwarding. This forwarding can be mapped to a fixed external URI or a Proxy server or localhost for local VAS. For an end-to-end secured communication via the proxy server, the proxy server should offer the HTTP CONNECT method as specified in IETF RFC 2817. If UDP based VAS are desired, the approach using session resumption can also be used in conjunction with OpenVPN. For end-to-end secured communication over fixed external URI, the EVCC and the target VAS server should negotiate a separate security association, e.g. a separate TLS session. The specific security for VAS is not in the scope of this document.",
            "block_bbox": [
                68,
                446,
                1054,
                630
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    68.0,
                    446.0
                ],
                [
                    1054.0,
                    446.0
                ],
                [
                    1054.0,
                    630.0
                ],
                [
                    68.0,
                    630.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "NOTE 1 For detailed information on the realization, please refer to Annex G.",
            "block_bbox": [
                68,
                650,
                749,
                676
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    68.0,
                    650.0
                ],
                [
                    749.0,
                    650.0
                ],
                [
                    749.0,
                    676.0
                ],
                [
                    68.0,
                    676.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "NOTE 2 IETF RFC 2817 has been updated by IETF RFC 7230 (which is updated by IETF RFC 8615) and IETF RFC 7231. These updates are considered to be included in this document.",
            "block_bbox": [
                68,
                697,
                1053,
                747
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    68.0,
                    697.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    697.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    747.0
                ],
                [
                    68.0,
                    747.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-2470] If the SECC does not support TLS session resumption, the EVCC shall setup a distinct TLS session for each value added service supported/provided by the SECC.",
            "block_bbox": [
                70,
                769,
                1053,
                823
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    70.0,
                    769.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    769.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    823.0
                ],
                [
                    70.0,
                    823.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "NOTE 3 For methods of associating a VAS session with a V2G session, see Annex G.",
            "block_bbox": [
                68,
                844,
                802,
                870
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    68.0,
                    844.0
                ],
                [
                    802.0,
